# Percentage scaling preserves the other operand unit

Verifies a percentage combined with a qualified length keeps the length subtype. Scaling 8m by 12.5% in both operand orders produces 1.000m: the percentage contributes only its hundredth scale while the meter unit survives.

>>> source
length: decimal = 8m
ratio: float = 12.5%
print(length * ratio)
print(ratio * length)

<<< stdout
1.000m
1.000m

<<< stderr
